 "notes": "99% CL exclusion contour (solid black line) from Fig. 2 of the paper, digitised from the raster figure Sigma_plot.png in the arXiv e-print via connected-component extraction and skeleton tracing; axes calibrated on the log decade ticks. The contour is the boundary of the excluded island in the (m_a, g_agamma) plane; it is open at the top of the plotted range (both branches reach the plot edge at g ~ 5e-10 GeV^-1), so the points trace the path from the low-mass top-edge endpoint (m ~ 1.2e-7 eV) down around the minimum (g ~ 3.1e-12 GeV^-1 at m ~ 4.5e-8 eV, consistent with the quoted g = 3.0e-12 at m_a ~ 40-50 neV) and up to the high-mass top-edge endpoint (m ~ 8.6e-7 eV). The paper quotes this main result at 99% CL (the 95% dashed contour and CTA/mock projections are not used). Limit is from photon-ALP oscillations in the Perseus cluster magnetic field (Ajello et al. model, B0 = 10 uG), independent of the local dark-matter density.",
